From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:39:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Cache EnumDirection.values() across NMS hot paths

Replace 26 remaining EnumDirection.values() call sites with the
package-visible cached array EnumDirection.n (contents and order
identical - the static initializer fills n by each constant's index,
which matches declaration order). values() clones the backing array on
every call, so hot loops were allocating repeatedly:

- World light BFS removal phase and neighbor-level calculation: one
  clone per visited node in both propagation passes
- BlockRedstoneWire x4, BlockRedstoneTorch x2, BlockDiodeAbstract x2,
  BlockPiston x2 (redstone updates)
- BlockFire x2 (fire spread), Chunk, BlockFluids, BlockIceFrost,
  EntityShulker, PathfinderWater, etc.

All sites are read-only iterations (verified: no array element
writes). Extends the earlier EnumDirection.a(Random) fix to the whole
NMS package, mirroring Lithium/Gale values() caching.

